<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ratnagiri (Odisha)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th–13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratnagiri">Ratnagiri</a> is a Buddhist site in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jajpur">Jajpur</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, part of the 'Diamond Triangle' with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitagiri">Lalitagiri</a> and Udayagiri. From about the 5th to the 13th century it was a major monastery and a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vajrayana">Vajrayana</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, flourishing under the Bhauma-Kara kings. Excavations have revealed monasteries, a large stupa and many sculptures.</p></div>
